WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.887
A pivot can be planned with four decisions.

00:00:03.887 --> 00:00:06.192
First, define the output row grain.

00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:11.192
Second, identify the category values that should become columns.

00:00:11.192 --> 00:00:17.437
Third, choose the measure. Fourth, choose the aggregate needed to fill each cell.

00:00:17.437 --> 00:00:21.957
For the diagnosis example, one output row is one month, the categories are diagnoses,

00:00:21.957 --> 00:00:26.842
and the measure is admission count.

00:00:26.842 --> 00:00:34.527
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:34.527 --> 00:00:38.412
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:38.412 --> 00:00:44.252
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:45.637
combination.
